-- title:
--   Points of the local Hecke algebra from congruent eigensystems
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ be a natural number and $S$ a set of natural numbers, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation domain which is adically complete for its maximal ideal. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and let $\theta : \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ be a ring homomorphism to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. Assume `HasIntegralStructure N 2`, i.e. that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice spanned by the weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space. Let $T$ be a commutative local ring equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure whose structure map is a local homomorphism, and let $\pi' : \mathbb{T} \to T$ be a ring homomorphism whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $T$ agrees with $\theta$ followed by the induced map of residue fields, that is, $\operatorname{residue}_T(\pi'(t)) = \mathrm{ResidueField.map}(\mathcal{O} \to T)(\theta(t))$ for all $t \in \mathbb{T}$. Then there exists an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $f$ from `heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`, the localisation of the base-changed Hecke algebra at the image of the complement of the prime `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ`, to $T$ such that $f$ is a local homomorphism and $f(\pi(t)) = \pi'(t)$ for every $t \in \mathbb{T}$, where $\pi$ is the structure map `heckeLocal.π`. Only existence is asserted, not uniqueness.
--
--   This is the representability property of the local Hecke algebra $\mathbb{T}_\theta$ attached to a residual eigensystem $\theta$: every eigensystem with values in a local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is congruent to $\theta$ factors through $\mathbb{T}_\theta$ by a local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map. It is used in the construction of the Hecke-algebra-valued Galois representation data, where the Hecke eigensystem of a given modular form or of an auxiliary deformation ring quotient must be realised as a point of $\mathbb{T}_\theta$.
-- source:
